From b052e78cdfb4151eebd24a60700853d229e08af3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CrockMr <118761873+CrockMr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:17:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose scene-setup commands, readiness and save refusal in
 the oracle adapter

Implements the KenshiOracle scene-setup contract (docs/scene-setup.md,
adapter 0.11.0) behind --oracle.

- setup_info, setup_area_census, setup_spawn_squad, setup_set_relation
  and setup_heal with the contract's parameter texts, gate order
  (world ready, probe load_save of this world epoch, allow_setup, then
  paused/no run_until and autosave for mutations, then a player) and
  refusal texts; replies carry exactly the contract keys, Meitou-only
  facts in engine_detail. No save-name allowlist.
- load_save accepts allow_setup; the opt-in takes effect when that load
  finishes, any other load clears it, a failed load keeps the gate shut.
  world_mutated is set before a mutation and cleared by a probe load.
- Spawns are planned before any change: a unique character is refused
  without consuming the spawn serial behind rng_key.
- Ping: plugin_version from OracleProtocol.AdapterVersion (0.11.0),
  capabilities, state_schema_version, world_readiness (no window),
  world_mutated and build_commit from the new OracleBuildCommit assembly
  metadata (full commit, or "unknown" without git or with local changes).
- Oracle mode drops every key, menu and import save/load request.
- issue_order orders only loaded squad members, refuses a dead target,
  a dead actor or an actor that is its own target, and replies
  affected_characters (characters kept for one release).
- docs/oracle.md documents the commands; OracleSetupTests covers the
  gate, the probe-load rule, readiness keys, spawn keys, the ping
  version and the player-faction spawn refusal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
